<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <!-- NuGet packaging metadata -->
    <PackageId>SharedKernel.Primitives</PackageId>
    <Version>1.1.0</Version>
    <Authors>Gresta-Vertex-Labs</Authors>
    <Company>Gresta-Vertex-Labs</Company>
    <Product>Platform.SharedKernel</Product>
    <Description>Foundational primitives for the SharedKernel: Result&lt;T&gt;, Error, ErrorCodes, IClock, SmartEnum, ValidationResult. Zero external dependencies. AOT-compatible.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>1.1.0 (WO-059 / P-384):
- Added ErrorType.Forbidden (= 7, next sequential value after BusinessRule = 6) and the corresponding Error.Forbidden(string code, string message) factory, mirroring BusinessRule's addition pattern (P-042). Forbidden represents a caller who is generally permitted to attempt an operation, but for whom this specific instance/condition is not satisfied — maps to HTTP 403 Forbidden at the presentation layer. Distinct from Unauthorized (not permitted to attempt this at all — HTTP 401) and from BusinessRule (a domain invariant violation, not an authorization/permission gate).
- Purely additive: no existing ErrorType member's numeric value changed and no existing Error factory's signature changed.
- COMPILE-TIME RISK: a downstream consumer with an exhaustive switch/switch expression over ErrorType carrying no discard/default arm will fail to compile after upgrading to this version, because a new enum member now exists. This is a compile-time signal, not a runtime break — add a discard/default arm or an explicit Forbidden case to restore exhaustiveness.
- No new ErrorCodes constant added — unlike BusinessRule's companion ErrorCodes.Domain.RuleViolated, no consuming phase requested a shared code constant for Forbidden.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageTags>shared-kernel;result;railway-oriented;clock;smart-enum;aot</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Gresta-Vertex-Labs/platform-shared-kernel</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Gresta-Vertex-Labs/platform-shared-kernel</PackageProjectUrl>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2026 Gresta-Vertex-Labs</Copyright>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="9.0.5" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Exclude the nested test project from the main project's compilation -->
    <Compile Remove="SharedKernel.Primitives.Tests\**" />
    <EmbeddedResource Remove="SharedKernel.Primitives.Tests\**" />
    <None Remove="SharedKernel.Primitives.Tests\**" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
